{"name":"Rosy Cheeks","hex":"#dc506e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rosy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Rose-coloured.","Of any reddish hue from bright pink to the color of ruddy cheeks in a light-skinned person."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make pinkish in colour.","To present in a deceptively optimistic or positive light."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rosy"},{"term":"cheeks","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of cheek","Ass; sex."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of cheek"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheeks"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rosy","blocks":[{"text":"Rosy is a given name or nickname and, more rarely, a surname. It may refer to:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosy"},{"title":"Cheek","blocks":[{"text":"The cheeks constitute the area of the face below the eyes and between the nose and the left or right ear. Buccal means relating to the cheek. In humans, the region is innervated by the buccal nerve. The area between the inside of the cheek and the teeth and gums is called the vestibule or buccal pouch or buccal cavity and forms part of the mouth. In other animals, the cheeks may also be referred to as \"jowls\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Cheek.jpg/330px-Cheek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheek"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm